+# Reminders
+
+For whoever changes pickup reminders, or proposes sending them by email to save the SMS cost. The day before pickup,
+larder sends each member a reminder of their pantry order's pickup slot, by SMS. A trial of email reminders in 2025
+doubled missed pickups, and members threw away less food once the reminders went back to SMS.
+
+## Message
+
+`remind` in `larder/reminders.py` sends the member one message, "Your pantry order is ready for pickup" and the
+slot, the day before pickup.
+
+## Channel
+
+Reminders go by SMS, `CHANNEL` in `larder/reminders.py`; the code can also send them by email. SMS costs the pantry
+about 40 euros a month, and email would cost nothing, so volunteers keep proposing the switch: [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md) in September
+was the third proposal that year.
+
+Email was tried from April to June 2025. The email provider reported that 34% of the reminder emails were never
+opened, and missed pickups rose from 6% of pantry orders to 13%. A missed pickup leaves a packed bag behind, and the
+fresh food in it is thrown away at closing time. Many members share one phone with their family and never check
+email; an SMS they see. Reminders went back to SMS on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups were back to 6% by August.
+
+A proposal to save the SMS cost has to answer those missed pickups and the food thrown away with them.
